WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.397
"The Best Source and Dose of
Plant Sterols for Lowering Cholesterol"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.440
Despite the vast literature
on phytosterols

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.880
lowering blood
cholesterol levels,

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.880
there is to date
no study investigating

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.960
the ultimate proof of efficacy:

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.360
the lowering of the incidence
of coronary heart disease.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.920
This is probably the strongest
argument against them.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.160
There are no studies
with hard endpoints

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.040
to confirm that the drop
in LDL cholesterol

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.880
from plant sterols translates
to a drop in heart attacks.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.200
The reason is
that even if people start out

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.880
with a ten-year cardiovascular
disease risk of ten percent,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.680
you'd have to randomize
about 30,000 people

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.200
to phytosterols for a decade
to detect such an effect.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.240
And at a more reasonable
ten-year risk of five percent,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.920
you might have to enroll
more than 300,000.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.920
Now, one could argue
that the cholesterol lowering

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.440
is all we need to know,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.880
since basically lowering
LDL cholesterol by any means

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.280
appears to lower
cardiovascular risk,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.400
whether by statins,
other kinds of drugs,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.800
diet, or surgery.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.720
However, there was a big trial
of extended-release niacin

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.720
in a group of patients with LDLs
starting down in the low 60s,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.880
and researchers saw
a further 10-point drop

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.840
after a few years

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.040
that should have dropped
the risk by at least 5 or 6%

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.480
but failed to offer

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.960
a statistically significant
benefit in the end.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.720
So, there's at least one example

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.920
of that line of argument
failing.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.680
There is that ezetimibe

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.160
that does have
a similar mechanism of action

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.840
as phytosterols—that is,
blocking cholesterol absorption.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.800
It partially blocks the
cholesterol absorption receptor;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.640
so, cholesterol absorption
is reduced by about 50%.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.320
When it was put to the test,

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.640
it did indeed
significantly improve

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.480
cardiovascular outcomes.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.480
And the 13-point drop in LDL

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.640
achieved by blocking
cholesterol absorption

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.160
with the drug is almost
the exact same drop in LDL

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.080
we'd expect from blocking
cholesterol absorption

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.680
with phytosterols,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.760
based on more than 100
randomized controlled trials.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.160
Does blocking
cholesterol absorption work

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.200
even if you don't eat
any cholesterol?

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.040
Yes, because the bulk
of the cholesterol

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.960
flowing through
our digestive tract

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.480
is dumped there
from our liver's own production.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.640
It also works for those
on statin drugs.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.800
In fact, adding two grams
of phytosterols a day

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.880
to your routine
may be equivalent

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.000
to like quadrupling
your statin dose.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.040
So, if you are going
to try phytosterols

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.640
to lower your LDL level,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.600
what's the best dose
and what's the best source?

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.880
The recommended daily dosing

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.560
is between
two to three grams a day,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.280
based on dose-response curves
like this,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.920
where the benefit
appears to plateau

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.120
at about those
two or three daily grams.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.880
There's a comparable
benefit curve

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:50.480
with plant stanols
which are similar molecules.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.800
Plant sterols and stanols
are absorbed better

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.320
if taken with meals,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.080
because the maximum
cholesterol load

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.440
to the intestine occurs
after gallbladder contraction

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.520
and delivery
of cholesterol-rich bile

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:02.960
to the intestine.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.880
Indeed, the same dose
of phytosterols

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.520
may have more than double
the LDL-lowering effect

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.160
when taken with meals
rather than between them

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.760
on an empty stomach.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.280
The full
LDL-cholesterol-lowering effect

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.520
can be detected
after just two weeks

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.360
and may last
as long as you take them,

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.240
but as soon as you stop,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.360
the cholesterol-lowering effect

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.320
will be lost
within a week or two.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.800
Phytosterols
in those kinds of doses

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.600
are available in supplements
and in fortified foods,

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.160
which lower LDL equivalently.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.360
As I talked about before,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.960
the margarines
are a total non-starter.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.400
Are there any healthy
phytosterol-fortified foods?

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.000
Not any that I could tell
where I live.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.680
In Australia there's a plant
sterol-fortified shredded wheat,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.960
but I don't know
if you can get it anywhere else.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.680
That leaves us
with supplements.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:56.240
It's always good to have
third-party certification

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.840
of authenticity,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.360
though I think
there's only one

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.840
USP-certified brand
at the moment,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.240
but ConsumerLab also tested
and approved three others.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.680
They're also pretty expensive;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.880
so, I was excited to see
that you can get it in bulk,

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.920
and you could presumably just
sprinkle a bit on your food,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.400
but that presumption
may be wrong.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.920
As a crystalline powder,

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.720
the free phytosterols
are much less efficient

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.640
at inhibiting cholesterol.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.960
That's why the initial studies
a half century ago

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.280
were using doses of, like,
10 to 20 grams a day.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.560
Then researchers figured out
how to make them more soluble

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.440
by making
fatty phytosterol esters,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.440
which is what you see
in the capsules.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.160
There are studies
suggesting that free sterols

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.440
block cholesterol absorption
as much as esterified sterols,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.480
but they included equal parts
of an emulsifier

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.400
to improve absorption.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.880
A study showing free sterols
could lower LDL

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.760
similarly relied
on some proprietary means

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.600
for solubilizing it.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.440
Just for fun, I tried taking
the bulk powder for a month

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.240
and, indeed,
sadly saw zero effect,

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.200
whereas I got
a nice 17 point drop in LDL

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.600
taking the exact same dose
in encapsulated ester form.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.040
Normally, I'm not a big fan
of lab tests,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.600
but if you do start
phytosterol supplements,

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.720
I would get
your cholesterol tested before

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.600
and after a month or so
on them.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.440
You should be able to get
your cholesterol tested

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.880
for free through your doctor,

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.720
but these days you can get
your cholesterol tested

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.200
at low cost or free
even without insurance

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.880
or a doctor visit.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.120
While some individuals
respond immediately

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.440
and get a major shift
in lipid profiles,

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.800
others are much more resistant
or even completely insensitive

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.280
to plant sterols,
or do even worse.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.880
Just because
the average response

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.680
is around a 10% drop
in LDL cholesterol,

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.720
maybe you'll be lucky
and respond even better.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.480
These are all
individual patients,

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.080
and this first person
saw a 38% drop!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.600
But it's also possible
you won't respond as well—

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.040
or, your cholesterol
may actually go up.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.480
That unfortunate person
at the end

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.040
had a 33% increase in LDL;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:09.000
so, even though
the average effect is good,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:15.000
you want to make sure
it's actually working for you.

